{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C", "description": "This source file implements a splitter for ELF-based firmware partitions, specifically designed to parse ELF kernel loader images in MTD devices for OpenWRT. It includes definitions for ELF headers, functions to read from memory technology devices, determine ELF image sizes, and to parse ELF structures to identify kernel and root filesystem partitions.", "external_files": ["<linux/module.h>", "<linux/init.h>", "<linux/kernel.h>", "<linux/slab.h>", "<linux/mtd/mtd.h>", "<linux/mtd/partitions.h>", "<linux/of.h>", "<linux/byteorder/generic.h>", "mtdsplit.h"], "external_methods": ["mtd_read", "mtd_find_rootfs_from", "register_mtd_parser"], "published": ["mtdsplit_elf_parse"], "classes": [{"name": "elf_header_ident", "description": "Represents the ELF identification structure containing magic, class, data encoding, version, OS ABI, and padding."}, {"name": "elf_header_32", "description": "Defines the ELF header structure for 32-bit ELF files, including type, machine, version, entry point, program header offset, section header offset, flags, header size, program header entry size, number of program headers, section header size, number of sections, and section header string table index."}, {"name": "elf_header_64", "description": "Defines the ELF header structure for 64-bit ELF files, with similar fields to the 32-bit version but with 64-bit offsets and addresses."}, {"name": "elf_header", "description": "Universal ELF header combining the identification and a union of 32-bit or 64-bit headers, depending on the ELF class."}, {"name": "elf_program_header_32", "description": "Represents the program header for 32-bit ELF files, including type, offset, virtual address, physical address, file size, memory size, and flags."}, {"name": "elf_program_header_64", "description": "Represents the program header for 64-bit ELF files, similar to the 32-bit version but with 64-bit address fields."}], "methods": [{"name": "int mtdspli